# Catalogue and price artifacts. These live on the Render persistent disk
# (render.yaml mounts it at /opt/render/project/src/data) and are rebuilt by
# scripts/build-phash-db.js. They were previously excluded by nobody ever
# running `git add` on them, which held until 24 Aug 2026 when `git add -A
# data/` swept 33 MB into a commit — including a card-prices.json that had
# been stale since May.
#
# Intent stated as a rule rather than as a habit.
data/card-db.json
data/card-prices.json
data/card-phashes.json
data/card-index-manifest.json

# Generated at runtime by pricing/adapters/cardmarket-url-store.js — resolved
# Cardmarket product URLs, so a restart does not re-pay a redirect service that
# fails transiently on roughly a third of cards.
#
# Deliberately NOT committed. data/ is where the Render persistent disk mounts,
# so a tracked copy would be shadowed by the disk and never read — the exact
# trap that silently disabled printedTotal disambiguation for weeks (see
# pricing/set-resolve.js). The store belongs ON the disk; it warms in one
# session and persists from there.
data/cardmarket-urls.json
data/cardmarket-urls.json.tmp
data/weekly-market/

# NOT ignored, and deliberately so: pricing/reference/pokemon-sets.json.
# It used to live in data/, where the disk mount shadowed it — see
# pricing/set-resolve.js. Reference data the code needs at runtime belongs
# beside the code, tracked, and outside any mount point.
